Join Axon and be a Force for Good.

At Axon, we’re on a mission to Protect Life. We’re explorers, pursuing society’s most critical safety and justice issues with our ecosystem of devices and cloud software. Like our products, we work better together. We connect with candor and care, seeking out diverse perspectives from our customers, communities and each other.

Life at Axon is fast-paced, challenging and meaningful. Here, you’ll take ownership and drive real change. Constantly grow as you work hard for a mission that matters at a company where you matter.

Your Impact

As an IT Support IV, you will serve as a senior technical resource for Axon’s manufacturing and warehouse operations at the Pinnacle Peak facility. You will help keep production, shipping, and logistics environments running by resolving complex endpoint and hardware issues, responding to manufacturing-critical incidents, and improving the tools and processes that support our employees and operations. This is a hands-on role with the opportunity to lead technical initiatives, mentor peers, and shape scalable IT support practices in a fast-paced environment where uptime matters.

What You’ll Do

Location: Onsite at our Pinnacle Peak Warehouse in Phoenix, Arizona &nbsp;
Core Hours: 8:00 a.m.-4:00 p.m.; flexibility to cover 6:00 a.m.-2:00 p.m. or 10:00 a.m.-6:00 p.m. shifts as needed &nbsp;
Reports to: IT Support Manager &nbsp;
Direct Reports: None &nbsp;

• Serve as the senior escalation point for IT support issues across the Pinnacle Peak manufacturing and warehouse location, as well as remote sites as needed. &nbsp;
• Diagnose and resolve complex hardware, software, and endpoint issues across Windows, macOS, mobile devices, production workstations, and specialized manufacturing peripherals. &nbsp;
• Respond rapidly to production-critical incidents, prioritize manufacturing outages appropriately, and minimize operational downtime. &nbsp;
• Deploy, image, configure, and lifecycle-manage manufacturing and warehouse devices using standardized endpoint-management and imaging processes. &nbsp;
• Support production, warehouse, and shipping operations by maintaining shipping stations, Zebra and production printers, logistics hardware, and specialized manufacturing devices. &nbsp;
• Partner with Manufacturing Engineering to support new production lines, equipment deployments, facility expansion projects, and production-readiness activities. &nbsp;
• Perform first-level troubleshooting for manufacturing network-connectivity issues, including basic DNS, DHCP, subnetting, and connectivity validation, before escalating infrastructure issues to Network Engineering. &nbsp;
• Maintain and troubleshoot enterprise systems and tools including Jamf, Microsoft Intune/Autopilot, Tanium, ServiceNow, Okta, Google Workspace, Zoom, Slack, and enterprise endpoint-management platforms. &nbsp;
• Own and improve onboarding and offboarding workflows in partnership with People Operations, Security, Endpoint Engineering, and IT Infrastructure. &nbsp;
• Lead the implementation of support tools, workflows, documentation, and automations that improve user experience, operational efficiency, and support scalability. &nbsp;
• Track and report on SLA adherence, incident trends, and recurring issues; use findings to drive continuous improvement and strengthen support processes. &nbsp;
• Collaborate with IT technicians globally, provide technical peer review and mentorship, and represent IT in cross-functional meetings and initiatives. &nbsp;
• Audit and reinforce IT policies, endpoint security practices, and compliance requirements in partnership with Information Security and relevant stakeholders. &nbsp;
• Support the sourcing, procurement, inventory, and maintenance of vendor hardware required for manufacturing and warehouse operations. &nbsp;

What You Bring

• 3-5 years of enterprise IT support experience, preferably in a manufacturing, warehouse, logistics, production, or similarly uptime-sensit

Technical Writer&nbsp;

Location: Hyderabad, India

OUR MISSION

At Redwood Software, we unleash human potential. We empower our customers with lights-out automation for their mission-critical business processes.

ABOUT US

Redwood Software is the leader in full-stack automation for mission-critical business processes. With the first SaaS-based composable automation platform specifically built for ERP, we believe in automation's transformative power. Our unparalleled solutions empower organizations to orchestrate, manage, and monitor their workflows across any application, service, or server - in the cloud or on-premise - with confidence and control.

CORE VALUES

One Team. One Redwood Make Your Own Weather Obsess over Customer Success Work the Problem Be Curious Own the Outcome Respect Each Other

YOUR IMPACT

As a Technical Writer at Redwood, you'll create and maintain documentation for our Tidal product line, working closely with product, engineering, and UX/design to keep customer-facing documentation and in-product content accurate and consistent.&nbsp;

You bring solid technical writing skills and sound judgment on ambiguous product or design questions. You're curious about applying AI tools to your own workflow, and comfortable partnering with designers and senior writers on content strategy. You'll follow and contribute to documentation and content design standards set by the team, and make structural or strategic content calls as they arise, looping in your lead on cross-team tradeoffs.

Documentation Development

• Write and maintain user guides, implementation documentation, developer content, and release notes for Tidal and Finance Automation, keeping pace with each release cycle.&nbsp;

• Produce API documentation (e.g., using Swagger/OpenAPI) for developer-facing endpoints as needed.&nbsp;

• Translate technical concepts - such as job scheduling and workload orchestration in Tidal, or financial close and reconciliation processes in Finance Automation - into content suited to administrators, developers, and business users.&nbsp;

• Keep existing documentation current as products change, verifying accuracy directly with engineering and product owners.

Content Design Collaboration

• Partner with UX/design on in-product content, UI text, tooltips, error messages, onboarding copy.

• Apply established content design principles (structure, findability, consistency) to your own documentation work.&nbsp;

• Identify and resolve content inconsistencies or gaps across docs and in-product text, looping in the team when a fix touches shared standards.

AI-Assisted Documentation&nbsp;

• Use approved AI tools to assist with drafting, editing, and structuring documentation, always reviewing AI-assisted output for accuracy before publishing.&nbsp;

• Identify and pilot opportunities to apply AI to documentation workflows, bringing outcomes back to the team.

Documentation Publishing &amp; Operations

• Publish and maintain documentation using the team's Git-based, docs-as-code workflow (Markdown, version control).&nbsp;

• Maintain metadata, organization, and versioning of published docs according to team standards.&nbsp;

• Update published content in response to product changes, customer feedback, and post-release review.

Team Collaboration

• Use Jira and Confluence within established team workflows.&nbsp;

• Participate in Agile ceremonies and deliver content aligned to sprint/release cycles.&nbsp;

• Communicate progress, blockers, and scope changes proactively so your lead can adjust priorities and timelines.&nbsp;

• Collaborate with SMEs and product stakeholders to verify technical accuracy.

YOUR EXPERIENCE

Required

• Bachelor's degree in Technical Communication, English, Computer Science, or equivalent practical experience.&nbsp;

• 3-5 years of technical writing experience for software products, ideally in B2B SaaS.&nbsp;

• Experience producing user guides, API documentation, and release notes in a fast-release

